A: Heavy on abstract jargon; "Destructive Forces" vs. "Creative Forces"; "God Energy"; a long process to create a "big ball" that "was not even a planet"; not any of the rules.
B: Simple and clear; Just two things "thought" in the hum; A thought about stillness, a thought about motion; they make a bargain; Olean breaks the crystal sphere, Vireth breathes on it, and crystals grow;
C: The First Light named "Elestra" and the twins "Teryn and Alara" and the "Ether Sea"; The "twin deities of Deniasent" who dance upon the surface of the Ether Sea, shaping it with each movement, shaping the land, mountains, sparking life into rocky crusts, carving rivers and lakes;
D: The three of them created the world to create a home in which to be, and so creation began. The first creatures arose from the suffering of the great trio's needs. Waking in horror and confusion, these first beings fled in massive migrations, in search of home. New life was born as the many races of Deniasent came to be, for each race evolved a few generations after the initial races. This was the first world, which fell to destruction in a massive cataclysm long, long ago. After the first planet was destroyed, the gods created another.
E: The word was *Here*. And because the word required a place, the world of Deniasent came into being. The stone grew beneath it until the Listener could no longer walk from one end to the other in a single thought. So the Listener broke its silence into many pieces and buried them in the soil. From the smallest pieces sprang grasses. From the longer pieces grew trees. Those that had held questions became animals, restless and hungry, forever searching. Those that had held songs became birds.
